      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not familiar with sdk_version-vs-min_sdk_version.\n\nI\u0027m matching the other prebuilts from the LLVM toolchain build. I thought that setting sdk_version to \"minimum\" meant that the prebuilt would be usable for any currently-supported API level (e.g. API 16+). The libunwind.a prebuilt is linked into (AFAIK) APEXs that target Q. Both the libunwind.a and libunwind-exported.a prebuilts are linked into the com.android.runtime (Bionic) APEX, but IIRC that\u0027s not currently an updatable mainline module.\n\nThe build/soong/scripts/update-apex-allowed-deps.sh script added the prebuilt_libunwind line. I don\u0027t know what \"no version\" here means, but some of the other similar prebuilts (e.g. prebuilt_libclang_rt.builtins-*-android, libgcc, libgcc_stripped) have the same \"no version\" marker.\n\nOTOH, two other variants of the LLVM unwinder have different markers:\n * libunwind_llvm(minSdkVersion:apex_inherit)\n * ndk_libunwind(minSdkVersion:16)\n\nndk_libunwind is a prebuilt of the arm32 LLVM unwinder that comes from the NDK. It works with API16 and up, but it\u0027s explicit about that. libunwind_llvm is built from external/libunwind_llvm, and is mostly irrelevant after my changes.",
